 special way because we  bring it to the middle of the table with  a wide variety of sauces and side dishes  the covers carve the meat on hot plates  hot cast-iron plates and the meat is  cured on Messiah Spears and swords which  makes it very unique and great eating  all our meats are sourced locally meats  like chicken beef and lamb is all found  by local farmers in Kenya it is illegal  to hunt a wild game the only game that  one can be able to serve is what is  farmed in ranches one of them are farms  ostrich it's unique in flavor it's still  very gamey and it's a very popular in  our restaurant the other exotic meat is  a crocodile crocodile is farmed mainly  for its a skin you can get this in many  places around the world Yama Yama is a  part of Kenya's cuisine from way back  most of the communities in Kenya used to  do a lot of hunting and they used to  make their own homemade meals from meat  particularly the Maasai community in  Kenya whose diet is predominantly meat  so this caught on and has become a  popular delicacy in literally all parts  of Kenya and the carnival we've  introduced this as part of our menu to  visitors from fine abroad to try  something which is part of our culture  hi I'm Kalamazoo a producer for tasty  and this is my family's ranch located in  the mountains of Sultan Hamid Kenya on  the ranch we raise cows goat and sheep  today we're going to be preparing  samosas I'll barbecue for my uncle's  wedding we're expecting about a thousand  guests so we're gonna prepare two cows  seven goats and three sheep this style  of preparing and barbecuing meat is the  traditional Masai way of cooking  everything that is used to cook is found  here on the land the wood we use comes  from the acacia tree which grows  naturally in this environment we raise  the same animals that we end up eating a  lot of people are involved in wrangling  these animals because they can be quite  dangerous so you'll have a lot of people  either in the home or neighbors 